# Deeper Depths Compat
item.immersiveintelligence.bullet.component.windcharge.name=Wind Charge
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.windcharge=Wind Charge
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.windcharge.lore=How?
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.windcharge.desc=Condensed wind obtained from Breeze, wind charges knock targets back and apply slowness and suppression in small radius. Due to properties of the charge, it remains on the same level of potency regardless of the shell size.

# Thaumcraft Compat
item.immersiveintelligence.bullet.component.primordial_pearl.name=Primordial Pearl
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.primordial_pearl=Primordial Pearl
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.primordial_pearl.lore=Magical Oppenheimer
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.primordial_pearl.desc=A potent artifact containing vast magical power and nearly unlimited potential that is beyond the known magical and physical laws. Despite its small size, rules of physics dictate that compression of such matter by integrated detonator explosive can only result in unparraleled levels of destruction from sheer amount of energy unleashed at once.

item.immersiveintelligence.bullet.component.alumentum.name=Alumentum
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.alumentum=Alumentum
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.alumentum.lore=Alchemist's explosives
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.alumentum.desc=A very volatile fiery substance, Alumentum is smaller in radius compared to TNT, but contains more concentrated power. Being in explosive container allows to focus its explosive power, making it more destructive than otherwise hand-thrown Alumentum.

item.immersiveintelligence.bullet.component.bottled_taint.name=Bottled Taint
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.bottled_taint=Bottled Taint
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.bottled_taint.lore=Ruinous power
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.bottled_taint.desc=Moving the contents of the bottle into a shell allows to deliver the corruptive Taint at much longer distances than it is possible to throw the bottle manually. Spread forth magical corruption, now at long distances!

ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_core_thaumium=Thaumium
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_thaumium=Thaumium Core
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.ore_thaumium.lore=Thaumaturgicallymtallurgic
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_thaumium.desc=A result of infusing iron with raw magical energy. Harder and better than base iron, it is a good candidate for massproduced shells, provided you can make alchemical mettalurgy supply keep up with the industrial demands.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_core_core_voidmetal=Void Metal
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_voidmetal=Void Metal Core
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_voidmetal.lore=Thaumaturgicallymtallurgic
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_voidmetal.desc=Disturbingly slick and warm to the touch, easy to work like gold, becoming as hard as tungsten and harder when struck - Void Metal is an excellent choice for bullets. However, properties of the metal make it somewhat difficult for conventional explosives to detonate with proper force. Furthermore, you cannot retrieve this metal core despite its regenerative properties, as it becomes unuseable after hitting the target.

# Thaumic Augmentation Compat
item.immersiveintelligence.bullet.component.impetus.name=Impetus
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.impetus=Impetus
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.impetus.lore=Rift power in a can
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.impetus.desc=Dangerous byproduct of Flux Rifts, and not fully understood material or phenomena, full range of usages for Impetus is shrouded in mystery. However, "infusing" the shell with the Impetus energy very significantly magnifies and supercharges its lethality.
